{{also|Hinterland}}
==English==
{{was wotd|2015|October|5}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|hinderland||dated}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|de|Hinterland}}, from {{compound|de|hinter|Land|t1=behind|t2=land|nocat=1}}, cognate to {{cog|en|hinder||back, rear}} + {{m|en|land}}. First used in English in 1888 by {{w|George Chisholm}} in his work ''Handbook of Commercial Geography'' originally as {{m|en|hinderland}}, but the current spelling (following German) became more popular.<ref>{{cite-web|title=hinterland|url=https://www.britannica.com/science/hinterland|work={{w|Encyclopædia Britannica}}|accessdate=20 September 2019}}</ref> The term is characteristic of a [[thalassocracy|thalassocratic]] analysis of space (from the point of view of a nation, such as 19th-century Britain, with maritime supremacy).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈhɪntə(ɹ)ˌlænd/}}
* {{audio|en|en-au-hinterland.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}
# The [[land]] immediately next to, and [[inland]] from, a [[coast]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1961|month=August|title=New traffic flows in South Wales|journal=Trains Illustrated|page=492|text=In West Wales it has never been possible until recently to exploit the magnificent natural harbour of Milford Haven, for there was no industrial '''hinterland'''.}}
# The [[rural]] [[territory]] surrounding an [[urban]] area, especially a [[port]].
# A [[remote]] or [[undeveloped]] area, a [[backwater]].
#*{{quote-web|en|date=February 9 2021|url=https://www.bbc.com/culture/article/20210208-is-tom-hanks-part-of-a-dying-breed-of-genuine-movie-stars|work=BBC|title=Is Tom Hanks part of a dying breed of genuine movie stars?
|author=Christina Newland|passage=In the film, {{w|Tom Hanks|Hanks}} is a veteran traversing the Texas '''hinterlands''' during the Reconstruction period when he stumbles upon a lost young white girl ({{w|Helena Zengel}}) who only speaks {{w|Kiowa language|Kiowa}}, and is forced to undergo a dangerous journey to bring the orphan to her family.}}
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} That which is [[unknown]] or [[unexplored]] about someone.
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} Anything [[vague]] or [[ill-defined]], especially something that is ill understood.
#* abstract of '''2007''', Lesley Jeffries, Textual Construction of the Female Body:
#*: This approach utilizes concepts such as naming, describing, contrasting and equating to access the '''hinterland''' between structure and meaning, and to map out the subtle ways in which texts can naturalise the ideology of the perfect female form.

